  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Papua New Guinea Animal Disease Response and Capacity Building Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building and disease surveillance programs are important to ensure early detection and response to animal disease incidents. The Australian Government is working with Papua New Guinea improving surveillance and the capacity of animal health services to detect and respond to  mutually important diseases, including African swine fever, through the provision of technical and policy support.</narrative>
  </description>
